## Security checklist
PASS scope isolation: repository queries and SQL triggers bind workspace_id across skills, versions, scans, reviews, installations, invocations, candidates, source events.
PASS RBAC: GET routes require run:read; lifecycle and /learn writes require workspace admin through SkillsService.
PASS idempotency: learning_commands compare semantic payload fields and /learn compares persisted candidate semantics.
PASS optimistic concurrency: lifecycle writes require If-Match skill revision; revoke/quarantine/rollback also require installation_revision.
PASS SQL safety: C21 repositories use parameterized node:sqlite statements; raw SQL constraints are in migrations only.
PASS append-only facts: learning_commands and skill_invocation_facts have no repository update/delete path and migration update triggers block mutation.
PASS approved snapshot chain: install/invoke require approved version, matching snapshot hash, approve review, clean passed scan, and no secret findings.
PASS proposed skill scope: /learn candidate checks proposed_skill_id exists in the same workspace at API, repository, FK, and trigger layers.
PASS rollback semantics: rollback target must be same skill, approved/clean snapshot, and different from current version at API, repository, and SQL trigger layers.
PASS descriptor-only boundary: no real external connector/provider/MCP call, credential read, URL/PDF/file fetch, external install, or outbound message path is implemented.

